    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12724",
      "problem": "Consider the following compound predicates:\n\n$x$ is even **and** divisible by $5.$ \n\n$x$ is even **or** less than $6$.\n\nExpress these compound predicates above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $5$\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is less than $6$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land.$\" \n\nSo, the first sentence reads\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130221/assets/543231d89e27c23abf29dbb195472fb700e4e592083501c998c4c767291ce49f.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nMoreover, the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\" \n\nSo, the second sentence reads\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130221/assets/1711a4acca502468f30ada1c8813cad12f02bbfd303736b4f80e8d95d2e64b70.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\lor C.$",
